From cd3557ca0eb8977101ca42a7b5bdfb8d3bea841e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Billy Brumley <bbb@iki.fi>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 08:31:49 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] SSHKDF: refuse a digest that has no output to avoid infinite
 loop

The key derivation specified by SSH appends one digest per round until
it has enough key material.  With a zero-size digest, such as the NULL
digest, it leads to an infinite loop.

Check the digest size of the supplied digest algorithm and error out
if it is non-positive.

Fixes: 8d76481b189b "Implement SSH KDF"
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-mythos-5-2
Reviewed-by: Neil Horman <nhorman@openssl.org>
Reviewed-by: Tomas Mraz <tomas@openssl.foundation>
Reviewed-by: Paul Dale <paul.dale@oracle.com>
Reviewed-by: Eugene Syromiatnikov <esyr@openssl.org>
Merge-date: Tue Nov 24 16:26:39 2026
Merged-from: https://github.com/openssl/openssl/pull/33923
(cherry picked from commit dce11301ff54174df95b9d593bd873e8e50f0938)
Upstream: https://github.com/openssl/openssl/commit/cd3557ca0eb8977101ca42a7b5bdfb8d3bea841e
---
 providers/implementations/kdfs/sshkdf.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/providers/implementations/kdfs/sshkdf.c b/providers/implementations/kdfs/sshkdf.c
index af39ba9..126b31a 100644
--- a/providers/implementations/kdfs/sshkdf.c
+++ b/providers/implementations/kdfs/sshkdf.c
@@ -183,6 +183,11 @@ static int kdf_sshkdf_derive(void *vctx, unsigned char *key, size_t keylen,
         ERR_raise(ERR_LIB_PROV, PROV_R_MISSING_MESSAGE_DIGEST);
         return 0;
     }
+    /* each round concats a digest, so we need positive len */
+    if (EVP_MD_get_size(md) <= 0) {
+        ERR_raise(ERR_LIB_PROV, PROV_R_INVALID_DIGEST_SIZE);
+        return 0;
+    }
     if (ctx->key == NULL) {
         ERR_raise(ERR_LIB_PROV, PROV_R_MISSING_KEY);
         return 0;
